WEBVTT

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.150
Project Mew seeks to
conduct a search for Mew.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.860
Go was accepted as a member,
and finally became a Chaser.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.290
Though troubled by urgent summons,
he exchanged words of encouragement with Satoshi,

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.210
and headed toward the meeting place.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.420
At the port of Kaina City
in the Hoenn Region,

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.510
Go met up with Tokio and Shigeru...

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:31.300
...and reunited with Professor Hodaka
and his senior Chasers, Tsurugi and Asahi, at the lab.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:32.890
Then...

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:38.770
As Satoshi and Dande’s heated
Masters Tournament finals battle was starting...

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.610
The extremely short dry season
arrived much earlier than expected,

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:50.360
so we had to bring forward
our departure.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.990
I thank you for your prompt response
to our urgent summons.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:59.790
I can’t help but imagine
Mew laughing at our being put in disarray.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.500
We are currently headed
to a place called Faraway Island.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:10.630
Hurricanes and storm clouds
constantly cover the island,

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.260
making landing impossible.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.140
But the clouds clear once a year
for the dry season.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:20.440
Last year, around the center
of Table Mountain...

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.310
...we picked up
extremely strong psycho energy.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.520
Presuming it to have come from Mew,

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.030
I set up Project Mew.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:36.530
We Chasers will land on Faraway Island
and climb Table Mountain.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:39.750
At its center,
we will search for Mew.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:40.830
However!

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:45.130
The table mountain is surrounded
by turbulent wind currents,

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:47.590
making it impossible to
approach by air.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.970
We will land some distance away from it,
and head for the table mountain on foot.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.840
We’re about to fly
over the island.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.010
Brace for turbulence!

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.500
If anything happens,
report in immediately. Understood?

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:54.340
Chasers,
I pray you find success!

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.260
<i>Thank you, sir!</i>

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.150
All the Pokémon here
look so lively.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.950
A true Pokémon paradise.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:22.830
Let’s go.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:23.740
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.790
Go, turn on your sensor.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:30.540
Yes, ma’am.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.510
So... that’s your invention,

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.130
which Professor Hodaka
then went and upgraded?

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.050
Yeah.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:45.010
It picks up nearby psycho energy,
and transmits it to the lab.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:50.060
Then the lab compares it with the waveform
of Mewtwo, who I’ve met before.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:54.980
Mew and Mewtwo should have matching
psycho energy waveforms, after all.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.740
How’s it going,
Professor Hodaka?

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.700
It’s functioning properly.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.950
I’ll let you know if I find anything.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.960
That’s amazing!

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.830
Something you made
is being used in Project Mew!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:16.630
It just happened to be
my field of expertise.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.970
Ms. Asahi, your specialties are
molecular biology and geology, right?

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:22.260
Yes.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:26.850
I approach the many mysteries of Pokémon
from those two perspectives.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.770
Mr. Tsurugi,
your field is mountain ranges,

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:34.730
and you research the ecosystems of
Pokémon living in harsh conditions, right?

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.020
Yeah.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.440
Places no human has ever been
are his favorite.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:44.240
Attempting the impossible
is what he lives for.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.700
If we do meet Mew,
will you catch it?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.880
What would you do, Go?

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:56.500
Huh?

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.880
I can’t say for sure what I’ll do
until the moment comes...

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.380
...but I guess
I’d want to catch it.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.390
What if...

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.810
...just like we look for the Pokémon
we want to catch...

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:14.440
...Pokémon are also looking
for the right person to catch them?

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.610
Wouldn’t that be great?

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.700
You’re such a romanticist, Tokio.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.030
Sorry...

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.990
But I can’t rule out the idea.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.580
If Pokémon are like that,
then maybe Mew appeared before me...

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.250
...because it wanted me to catch it?

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.540
Don’t know if I’d say that.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.980
Whoa, out of nowhere?!

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.230
A Laglarge!

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.900
Then I’ve got
just the right Pokémon!

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.160
Magical Leaf!

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.880
You’re incredible, Tokio!

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.180
That’s a Viridion, right?!

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.810
Yeah, I caught it
during my Last Mission.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:34.180
Wow, you did?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:39.310
Viridion! Grassland Pokémon!
Grass/Fighting type!

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.570
A legend tells of this Pokémon
working together...

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:45.950
...with Cobalion and Terrakion
to protect the Pokémon of the Isshu Region!

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.700
That’s so cool!

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:49.870
Viridion!

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.580
Thank you.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.790
Let’s hurry on ahead.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.080
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.890
It’s that huge...?

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.350
And such a mystifying place...

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:15.980
Apparently ancient fishermen
called it “Sharishari-ma.”

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.060
“Sharishari”?

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.480
It’s the sound of the mountain’s evil spirits
eating humans.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:27.780
Meaning this is a fearsome mountain
to stay away from at all costs.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:32.990
It’s also a geologically
important mountain.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.790
Its topography hasn’t changed
for hundreds of millions of years.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:40.620
It may have been the center,
the core of the world since time immemorial.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.250
This is...

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.090
The center of the world...

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.840
This is Hodaka.
Can you hear me?

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.550
We hear you.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.060
The sensor has picked up
psycho energy!

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.560
And the waveform?

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.900
Professor Hodaka,
what was the waveform?

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.020
—can... ear...

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.110
Professor!

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:04.570
Huh...?

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.400
It cut off...

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.700
Same here.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:16.330
The sensor isn’t working, either...

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.330
My Smartphone Rotom...

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.660
No luck.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.040
Even my flashlight...

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.420
Not our Monster Balls, too?!

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.760
This can’t be real...

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.600
None of our devices
are working?

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.100
Looks like it.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:42.270
That means we can’t even recall these three
to their Monster Balls...

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.400
And behind this is...

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.150
...Mew?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:59.120
We weren’t able to
confirm the waveform,

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.330
but it definitely picked up
psycho energy.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.540
So, it came from near here?

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.050
Should we head back for now
and get reorganized?

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:14.930
If Mew is behind this,
we can’t let this chance get away.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:21.520
We no longer have the help of Pokémon
other than Manyula, Marilluri, and Sarunori.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.480
We use everything we currently have
and begin the climb.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.690
Understood?

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:27.940
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.530
Sarunori, let’s do our best!

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:35.700
Manyula and I will go first
and anchor the rope.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.700
Use that rope to follow us.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.950
Then I’ll be your backup.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.080
My backup will be Manyula.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:46.670
Shigeru, you climb behind us
and guide the followers.

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:47.590
Yes, sir.

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:51.710
I’ll be at the tail end
and ensure everyone stays safe.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.340
Please do.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.800
Following Shigeru
will be Tokio, then Go.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.100
Yes, sir!

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:59.700
I’m pathetic for always
relying on my Pokémon...

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.330
Shigeru, watch out!

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.120
Huh?

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.080
An Airm'd?!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:38.240
Looks like this is their territory.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.290
What do we do?

00:12:56.760 --> 00:13:00.800
We’ll take a different route
to the center!

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:03.300
Got it.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.430
We’ll keep heading up.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.140
Manyula,
you back up Shigeru.

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:10.640
Let’s go.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.560
Yes, ma’am.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.460
Thank you.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.630
What’s that...?

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.300
A waterfall?

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:52.850
If we so much as touch the stream,
it’ll send us falling headfirst...

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:55.190
Looks like we’ll have to turn back.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.190
What is it?

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.030
A cave...

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.790
We might be able to
go through there.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:42.820
Good work.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.200
So this is...

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:51.790
...Table Mountain’s summit...

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.420
This is just our starting point.
Let’s get to the center.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:57.210
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:03.470
Pokémon?

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:06.970
They’re Melecie.
Are they sleeping?

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.640
We don’t know
what dangers there could be.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.980
Everyone, stay vigilant.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:13.770
Yes, ma’am.

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.780
The center would be about here.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:35.330
What’s this?

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:38.580
An unnaturally perfect
round hole.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.300
Like it was made by someone...

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.090
Mew?

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:44.300
Yes.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.550
This will work.

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:49.220
I’ll check inside.

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:50.220
Right!

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:04.570
What happened?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.320
Kurabo Berries.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:08.820
And noticeably eaten.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.950
So a Pokémon was here?

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.200
It hasn’t been long since...

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:17.660
What?

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.210
Is something there?

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:21.840
Some sort of hair is stuck to it.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:23.210
A hair?

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.380
A very short, fine hair...

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.800
It might belong to Mew!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:29.590
Huh?!

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:36.060
When we get back to the lab,
we’ll run a DNA analysis.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:46.320
This is quite a strange space.

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:48.900
I wouldn’t have thought
it’d be this open...

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:53.450
There are the usual
cave Pokémon here,

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:58.040
but also so many fossil Pokémon
living wild...

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:03.670
This is likely a closed space
completely untouched by humans,

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:08.090
cut off from outside contact
for hundreds of millions of years.

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:11.720
There could be Pokémon
with unique biology here!

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.800
Mew comes first. Let’s go.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:14.890
Y-Yes, sir!

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:19.890
If Mew was the one eating
those Kurabo Berries from earlier...

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:22.650
...it could be down this cave!

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:24.440
Do you think it’ll appear to us?

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:25.730
Of course!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:32.030
But Mew doesn’t appear when it senses
the evil feelings of humans, right?

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:34.030
Don’t worry!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:36.790
We don’t have
any evil feelings at all, yeah!

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:41.290
Even if we get to see Mew,
don’t let your guard down.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:45.420
When Professor Hodaka
did research in various regions,

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.800
he found many reports
of Mew sightings.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:51.590
While some say
it was as merciful as an angel,

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.300
others call it as cruel as a demon.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.310
A demon?

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:00.060
Apparently a trainer chasing Mew
was slammed to the ground,

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.230
and had fire and cold
launched at them.

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:04.190
I don’t believe that!

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:08.030
That trainer must’ve done pretty bad things,
don’t you think?

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:15.950
It’s not here.

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:19.790
If we could at least find
some sort of trace of it...

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:23.870
Down there...

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.380
Looks like we can get through.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:30.460
I’ll check it out.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.470
Kabutops and Ptera!

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.850
Stand back, Shigeru!

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:47.560
Meet them with Crossroad Kill!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.200
Evil Pulse!

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.370
Now’s our chance!

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.120
Right!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.550
Solrock and Lunatone!

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:17.300
The Meteorite Pokémon,
said to have fallen from space?

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:21.180
Both of you, get behind me!

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:22.560
Yes, ma’am!

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.280
Marilluri! Light Screen!

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:41.160
Sarunori!

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.580
Hydro Pump!

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:57.340
Go, Tokio, follow me!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.220
Yes, ma’am!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.810
Sarunori, you okay?

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:09.690
Good to hear it.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:22.950
Mr. Tsu—

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:23.990
Something’s here!

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.480
Groudon?!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.490
An underground lake...

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:05.410
Look! We might just be able
to pass through there!

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:07.290
We have no choice but to try.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:08.160
Yes, ma’am!

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.730
Kaiogre!

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.980
Suddenly, the Legendary Pokémon
Groudon appears...

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.980
...along with Kaiogre.

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.780
Will Go and the others
be able to encounter Mew...

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:41.200
...somewhere on this
enigmatic island?!

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:09.580
Now, off to the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.830
Go!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:14.540
The sensor is responding!

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:19.500
There’s no way to calm Mew down
but to battle it!

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:20.960
You’re still going?!

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:22.800
Mew can be an angel or a demon!

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:25.840
If we let it keep rampaging,
the other Pokémon will be in danger!

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:30.260
I’ve longed to see you again,
but not like this!

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:32.520
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:34.390
Taking the Future in Hand!

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:36.690
Here we go!

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:38.770
Championing the evils of truth and love!

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:40.520
Team Rocket Explorers!

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:44.780
Following an order
to catch new Pokémon...

00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:47.610
...we made our first visit
to the Paldea Region.

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:50.160
Oh, meow?
There’s one, meow!

00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:52.040
I think that one’s...

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:55.040
The Grass Cat Pokémon,
Nyahoja.

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:59.670
It says it sulks if it sees its trainer giving attention
to a Pokémon other than itself.

00:23:59.670 --> 00:24:01.800
You like to sulk too, Nyarth!

00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:03.420
When Sakaki’s with his Persian—

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:04.670
How rude, meow!

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:07.630
That doesn’t bother me at all,
you hear, meow?!

00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:09.760
Well, let’s catch it quick!

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:10.800
Yeah!

00:24:13.310 --> 00:24:15.100
Huh? What’s that?

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:16.690
What a great aroma...

00:24:16.690 --> 00:24:18.730
Don’t fall asleep, meow!

00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:24.820
<i>What an awful feeling...</i>

00:24:24.820 --> 00:24:26.360
Today’s roundup!

00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:27.200
Nyahoja has...

00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:28.820
...such a great scent!
